   "evidence": "Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean:224 `transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiVolumeForm : L.transverseEpsRaise minkowskiVolumeForm _ = ...` (token = the four-form) vs :250 `transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiProduct_transverseEpsRaise (\u03b5 : Vector 3 [\u22c0^Fin 4]\u2192\u2097[\u211d] \u211d)` (token = the metric, \u03b5 is a parameter). The repo's existing marker use, `finrank_transverse_minkowskiProduct_eq_two` (:183), disambiguates against a general-`B` lemma (`finrank_transverse_add_two_eq`); grep shows no such counterpart for the square.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the ambiguous marker from these two: `transverseEpsRaise_comp_self` for the `\u2218\u2097` form and `transverseEpsRaise_comp_self_apply` (or `transverseEpsRaise_transverseEpsRaise`) for the pointwise form. Neither name is taken \u2014 the general-`B` theory in Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/LightConeBasis.lean has no square lemma \u2014 so no disambiguating marker is needed here.",
   "issue": "`transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiProduct_transverseEpsRaise` (250) and `transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiProduct_comp_self` (264) put `minkowskiProduct` (the raising metric) in exactly the name slot where the parallel `transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiVolumeForm_transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiVolumeForm` (234) and `transverseEpsRaise_minkowskiVolumeForm` (224) put the four-form argument, so the names read as the \u03b5-at-`minkowskiProduct` statements, which is type-incorrect. The two names for the same fact also share no suffix (`_transverseEpsRaise` vs `_comp_self`).",
   "line": "250"
  }
 ],
